      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 5-year-old boy underwent ventricular septal defect closure as well as resection of the muscle bundle of a double-chamber right ventricle and a subaortic membrane. Five days after surgery, echocardiography revealed a left anterior descending artery fistula with 2 sites of entry to the right ventricle. The child was asymptomatic with no murmurs. Echocardiography is an excellent tool for detecting such silent clinical lesions."},
